The agent works — I've verified the decision logic end to end against a live model (rebook on the right booking, dry-run safe, no compensation when not payable, 429 retries working). Now build the case record — this is a required deliverable.

After the agent finishes a case, produce a structured record capturing all six required things:

the decision and what the passenger gets;
the reasoning, and what it rests on (which facts, which policy clauses from the entitlements service);
what was consulted (every read tool call made);
what was actually done — every write action, and whether it was real or dry-run;
anything still uncertain;
what a human still needs to do, if anything (including any escalation raised).

Emit each record two ways: a machine-readable record.json and a human-readable record.md, written to an output/<case-id>/ folder. Build the record from the tool-call trace the agent already captures, so it reflects what actually happened, not a re-description. Also make a top-level runner that can work all twelve cases in one command and drop all their records into output/, plus print a short summary line per case (decision + total paid + escalated yes/no).

Keep dry-run on. Show me the record.json and record.md for case-01 when done — I'll review the shape before we run the full sweep.

